 "content": "# ARC pattern note: square-frame nested distance colors\n\nObserved in task-c8d4ed50. Input is a 15x15 canvas with a 7x7 hollow interior framed by color 3 (the frame itself is rows 3 and 11, columns 4 and 12 in 1-based grid coordinates). A single interior 3 acts as a marker. Fill the other 48 cells of the 7x7 interior according to Chebyshev distance from the marker (distance = max(abs(row-marker_row), abs(col-marker_col))): distance 1 -> color 4; distance 2 -> color 2; distance 3 -> color 4; distance 4 -> color 2; and so on, alternating outward. Keep the marker as 3 and preserve the outer 3 frame and background 0s. Thus every square Chebyshev ring about the marker alternates 4,2,4,2,...; clip rings at the 7x7 interior boundaries. The marker may be off-center, so compute distance from its actual location rather than assuming a centered pattern. The examples included marker at (4,4), (6,2), and (1,6) in 1-based interior coordinates; test had marker at (3,1)."
